Subject: Fail the build on upstream ctest failures except the two network-only DAP4 tests
Description: Debian's override_dh_auto_test ends with `|| echo "Ignoring test failures"`, so any failing upstream ctest passes silently. This patch removes that mask so a regression in the 221 local tests fails the build. The two dap4 tests named in the exclusion list fetch from remotetest.unidata.ucar.edu or need the d4ts test server, which the hermetic builder cannot reach, so they are excluded by name instead of masked.
Origin: DHI-internal (DHI build policy for this rebuild)
Base-Tree: debian netcdf 1:4.9.3-1
Forwarded: not-needed (DHI build policy, not an upstream change)
Drop-When: never: DHI requires a failure-fatal upstream test gate and Debian masks test failures by design
Verify: test debian/rules

--- a/debian/rules
+++ b/debian/rules
@@ -35,7 +35,7 @@
 		-DHDF5_LIBRARY_PATH=$(HDF5_LIBRARY_PATH)
 
 override_dh_auto_test:
-	ARGS="--output-on-failure" dh_auto_test --max-parallel=1 || echo "Ignoring test failures"
+	ARGS="--output-on-failure -E 'dap4_test_test_(remote|dap4url)'" dh_auto_test --max-parallel=1
 
 execute_after_dh_auto_install:
 	# Strip RPATH
